# Roshanfer Artifact Evaluator Configuration
# EuroSys 2027 Artifact Evaluation
#
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Copy this file: cp evaluator.env.example evaluator.env
# 2. Edit evaluator.env with your settings (DO NOT edit this example file)
# 3. Source before running: source evaluator.env
# 4. Or add to .envrc for automatic loading: echo "source_env evaluator.env" >> .envrc

# =============================================================================
# CloudLab Configuration
# =============================================================================

# Your CloudLab username (used for SSH and parsing manifests)
# Example: EVALUATOR_CLOUDLAB_USER="alice"
EVALUATOR_CLOUDLAB_USER="your_cloudlab_username"

# CloudLab manifest path (download from CloudLab portal after instantiation)
# This is passed to --cloudlab-manifest when using --remote mode
# Example: EVALUATOR_CLOUDLAB_MANIFEST="$HOME/downloads/manifest-12345.xml"
EVALUATOR_CLOUDLAB_MANIFEST="$HOME/cloudlab-manifest.xml"

# =============================================================================
# Docker Registry Configuration
# =============================================================================

# Docker Hub username or registry prefix for container images
# If using DockerHub: set to your DockerHub username (e.g., "myuser")
# If using private registry: set to full prefix (e.g., "myregistry.io/myuser")
#
# IMPORTANT: You must have push access to this registry!
#            Run "docker login" before building images.
#
# Example: EVALUATOR_DOCKER_REGISTRY="alice_dockerhub"
EVALUATOR_DOCKER_REGISTRY="your_dockerhub_username"

# =============================================================================
# Control Node Configuration
# =============================================================================

# The "control" machine IP/hostname where Prometheus, OTEL, and ingress run
# In CloudLab mode: typically the first generator node's IP (get from manifest)
# In local mode: typically 192.168.1.100 or your local machine's IP
#
# This IP is used for:
# - Prometheus pushgateway (port 9091)
# - OTEL collector (port 4317)
# - K6/wrk2 target endpoints (ports 2000, 3000)
#
# Example: EVALUATOR_CONTROL_IP="128.110.217.45"
EVALUATOR_CONTROL_IP="192.168.1.100"

# =============================================================================
# SSH Configuration (Optional)
# =============================================================================

# SSH user for Kubernetes cluster setup (K3s installation on remote nodes)
# Default: uses EVALUATOR_CLOUDLAB_USER, or falls back to "ubuntu"
# Override if your CloudLab profile uses a different default user
#
# Example: EVALUATOR_SSH_USER="cc"
# EVALUATOR_SSH_USER="${EVALUATOR_CLOUDLAB_USER:-ubuntu}"

# SSH key path (optional, auto-detected from ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 or ~/.ssh/id_rsa)
# Only set if using a non-standard key location
#
# Example: EVALUATOR_SSH_KEY="$HOME/.ssh/cloudlab_rsa"
# EVALUATOR_SSH_KEY="$HOME/.ssh/id_ed25519"

# =============================================================================
# Advanced (usually no changes needed)
# =============================================================================

# Number of generator nodes (for --remote mode; overridden by --num-generators flag)
# Default: 3 (as used in paper evaluation)
# EVALUATOR_NUM_GENERATORS=3

# Image tag for Docker builds (default: "ae" for artifact evaluation)
# Override to use a different tag for your builds
# EVALUATOR_IMAGE_TAG="ae"

# =============================================================================
# Notes
# =============================================================================
# - Do NOT commit your evaluator.env to git (it's in .gitignore)
# - Keep this evaluator.env.example file as reference
# - For CloudLab experiments, run with --remote flag and this config
#   Example: ./run_tests.sh --remote --num-generators 3 --config configs/tests/one-service
